hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1318","`Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We have no heirs; whatever (wealth) we leave behind is charity."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would take from this wealth the expenses for his family for a year, and whatever remained after that, he would spend it in those places where Allah's wealth, that is, charity, is spent. Then (Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) said to the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) sitting with him: I ask you by Allah, by whose command the heavens and the earth are established (tell me!), do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said this? They said: Indeed, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said this. And in that gathering were Sayyiduna Ali, Abbas, Uthman, Abdur Rahman bin Awf, Zubair, and Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with them). And the full narration regarding the dispute between Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib and Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with them) was mentioned, the bringing of which is not among our duties. (In Surah Al-Anfal: 41, there is mention of khums. The chapter points to this, and see the hadith in the Book: Explanation of Faith... Chapter: Paying the fifth part of the spoils of war is part of faith.)"
"1319","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he produced two shoes made of hairless leather before the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them), which had two straps each, and stated that they were the shoes of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1320","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) took out a sheet (which) is called ""Malbada"" and said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away while wearing this."
"1321","In one narration, it is reported from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she took out a thick waist-wrapper, the kind that the people of Yemen make, and a sheet of the same kind, which is called ""mulabbada"" (saying that these belonged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1322","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the cup of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke, he (peace be upon him) fastened a silver wire at the broken place."
"1323","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a child was born to one of us, so he named him Qasim. The Ansar said, ""We will never call you Abu al-Qasim, nor will we cool your eyes (by this blessed title)."" So that person went to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! A boy has been born to me, and I have named him Qasim, but the Ansar say, 'We will not call you Abu al-Qasim, nor will we cool your eyes.'"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The Ansar have done well. Take my name, but do not take my kunyah (title), because I am the Qasim."" (Qasim means the one who distributes.)"
"1324","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Neither do I give you (anything) nor do I withhold from you; I am only a distributor, I spend wherever I am commanded."
"1325","Sayyida Khawla Ansariya (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Some people dispose of Allah's wealth without right; for them, there will be Hell on the Day of Resurrection."" (That is, they will enter Hell.) (Allahumma ajirna min an-naar)"
"1326","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One of the Prophets among the earlier Prophets fought in a battle. He said to his people: 'No one should go with me who has married a woman and wishes to consummate the marriage but has not yet done so, nor anyone who has built a house but has not yet put its roof on, nor anyone who has bought sheep or camels and is waiting for them to give birth.' So he fought in the battle. When they reached near a town at the time of Asr prayer or close to it, he said to the sun: 'You are subservient (to Allah) and I am also subservient (to Allah). O Allah! Hold it back for us.' So it was held back until Allah granted them victory. Then they gathered the spoils of war. A fire came down from the sky to consume the booty, but it did not consume it. So the Prophet said: 'Someone among you has stolen (from the booty), so let one man from each tribe pledge allegiance to me.' The hand of one man stuck to his hand, so the Prophet said: 'The thief is among you, so let all the people of your tribe pledge allegiance to me.' Then the hands of two or three men stuck to his hand. The Prophet said: 'You have committed the theft.' So they brought a head of gold shaped like a cow's head and placed it there. Then the fire came and consumed it. Then Allah saw our weakness and our inability, so He made the spoils of war lawful for us."
"1327","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army towards Najd in which Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was also present. They found many camels as war booty, so each of them received twelve or eleven camels as their share, and one camel was given to them in addition to their share."
"1328","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was distributing the war booty at (the place of) Ji‘ranah, a man said to him, ""Be just."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then I would be wretched if I do not act justly (if I do not do justice, then who will)?"
"1329","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him, his father) found two slave girls among the captives of Hunain and kept them in a house in Makkah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the captives of Hunain to be set free, so people started running in the streets. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to his son, ""O Abdullah! See what this is?"" He said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has set the captives of Hunain free (this is the reason)."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Go, you also set those two slave girls free."" (These slave girls had come to him from the spoils of war.)"
"1330","‘Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) says: While I was standing in the row on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and to my left and saw two young boys from the Ansar. So I wished that I were between (the strong horsemen) among them. Anyway, one of them pressed me and said, “O uncle! Do you recognize Abu Jahl?” I said, “Yes. But what do you want with him?” He said, “I have heard that he abuses the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). By Him in Whose hand is my soul, if I see him, then my body will not part from his body until the one of us whose death is decreed dies.” I was amazed at this. Then the other pressed me and spoke in a similar manner. Then, after a short while, I saw Abu Jahl running among the people. I said, “Listen! This is the person you were asking me about.” So both of them advanced towards him with their swords and struck him until they killed him. After that, they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, “Which of you killed him?” Each of them said, “I killed him.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Have you cleaned your swords?” They said, “No.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at their swords and said, “Indeed, you both killed him, but the spoils will go to Mu’adh bin ‘Amr bin Jamuh.” And those two boys were Mu’adh bin ‘Afra and Mu’adh bin ‘Amr bin Jamuh."
"1331","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) once said: ""I give (wealth) to the Quraysh (those who have newly embraced Islam) in order to win their hearts, because they are still close to the period of ignorance."
"1332","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): Some people from the Ansar presented themselves to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Allah granted His Messenger the spoils of Hawazin as much as He willed, the Prophet (peace be upon him) began giving some people from the Quraysh one hundred camels each. Some of the Ansar began to say, ""May Allah forgive the Prophet (peace be upon him); he is giving so much to the Quraysh and not giving to us, even though the blood of the disbelievers is still dripping from our swords."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this conversation of theirs was conveyed to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he called the Ansar and gathered them in a leather tent, and he did not call anyone else with them. When the people had gathered, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came and said, ""What is this matter that has reached me from you?"" The wise ones among them said, ""O Messenger of Allah! None of our wise people have said anything; rather, it was the younger ones among us who said this..."" The rest of this hadith will come later. (See the chapter: The Account of the Battle of Ta’if, which took place in Shawwal, 8 AH.)"
"1333","Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) says that while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and with him were those people who were returning from Hunain, the Bedouins began to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for things, until they pushed him towards a thorny tree, so much so that his cloak got caught in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and said: “Give me my cloak. If I had as many camels as these trees, I would distribute them among you, and you would never find me miserly, a liar, or faint-hearted.”"
"1334","'Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was walking with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and at that time, he was wearing a thick-edged Najrani cloak. Then a Bedouin caught hold of him and pressed him hard, so much so that I saw on the outer part of the blessed neck of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) the mark left by the edge of the cloak due to his forceful pulling. After that, the Bedouin said, ""Give me something from the wealth of Allah that you have."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards him and smiled, and then ordered that something be given to him.'"
"1335","Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when, on the day of Hunayn (the Battle of Hunayn), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave some people more (from the spoils of war) than others—such as giving Aqra' bin Habis one hundred camels, and giving 'Uyaynah (may Allah be pleased with him) the same amount, and giving some of the Arab chiefs more as well—a man said, ""By Allah! This is a distribution in which there has been no justice,"" or (he said), ""Allah's pleasure has not been intended in this."" So I said, ""By Allah, I will inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this."" So I went to him and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""If Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do not act justly, then who will act justly? May Allah have mercy on Musa (peace be upon him); he was harmed with even greater than this, and he was patient."
"1336","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): We used to find honey and grapes during our battles (for Jihad), so we would consume them at that time and would not keep them (to distribute later)."
